<article class="env-situation" id="0C61">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0C61">Situation <span data-tag="0C61">55.9.3</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $K$, residue field $k$, and uniformizer $\pi $. Let $C$ be a smooth projective curve over $K$ with $H^0(C, \mathcal{O}_ C) = K$. Let $X$ be a regular proper model of $C$. Let $C_1, \ldots , C_ n$ be the irreducible components of the special fibre $X_ k$. Write $X_ k = \sum m_ i C_ i$ as in Lemma <a href="/tag/0C5Z" data-tag="0C5Z">55.9.1</a>. </p>
